  "notes": "Where on a body a thing is worn, and what the doctor reports about worn things. The constants are data/item/wear.yml's places, head to foot, and its under table (a place beneath another: put on or taken off only while nothing is worn above it), and data/item/kits.yml's wear table (the place each kit name is worn on). A case gives a story and every row its records hold (records: stories, locations, characters, playthroughs, items); output is wear::findings for that story in item id order: {code, severity, remedy, subject: [table, id], message}. A thing belongs to its game's story, else its room's, else its holder's. A `wear` that is no place is wear_no_such_place; a worn thing with no wear is worn_unwearable; a worn thing nobody holds (in a room, the world's own row in no person's hands, or not intact) is worn_not_held; a second worn thing on one place by one body (one game's party or person, or a person in the world), after the first by id, is worn_place_taken. outer and body are two places.",
